{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369318-best-ways-to-streamline-2nd-edition-combat-2-0-or-2-5","id":1369318,"title":"Best ways to streamline 2nd Edition Combat? (2.0 &/or 2.5)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-21T03:35:09-08:00","id":1369318,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon12.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Best ways to streamline 2nd Edition Combat? (2.0 &/or 2.5)","content":"How have you (or others you know) streamlined &amp;/or simplified combat for either version of 2nd Edition?<br /> <br /> I want to run a game for two younger players.<br /> <br /> I've noticed that using a Battle Wheel makes the combat portion of the game feel more like a board game, which I like, but I'd like it to feel more like a speedy game then a long Monopoly game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T05:20:56-08:00","id":1369336,"title":"","content":"No flurries or multi-attacks allowed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T07:10:24-08:00","id":1369360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369318-best-ways-to-streamline-2nd-edition-combat-2-0-or-2-5?p=1369336#post1369336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No flurries or multi-attacks allowed.</div> </div> </div> </div>We just let the player roll once and apply the effects multiple times. Probably, ditching them altogether is easier, but may affect Charm trees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T07:13:01-08:00","id":1369362,"title":"","content":"2.5 nerfs perfects. We sort of went in-between, by having the costs stay the same as 2e but only allowing them to be used every other turn.<br /> <br /> We also doled out free Excellencies for any Abilities where you had 2+ Charms, so people can focus on other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T08:57:53-08:00","id":1369388,"title":"","content":"An advantage of 2e tick based combat over Ex3's initiative based combat when it comes to new players is that it's easier to keep record of the player's weapon speeds and hide the moving parts from them like a video game, tracking that information yourself and simply telling them whose turn it is now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T14:57:25-08:00","id":1369452,"title":"","content":"Stunts don't restore motes.<br /> Use Extras health levels on all NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T15:12:56-08:00","id":1369456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369318-best-ways-to-streamline-2nd-edition-combat-2-0-or-2-5?p=1369452#post1369452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stunts don't restore motes.</div> </div> </div> </div> Or wp.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Use Extras health levels on all NPCs. </div> </div> </div>This is good advice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T01:07:56-08:00","id":1369529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369318-best-ways-to-streamline-2nd-edition-combat-2-0-or-2-5?p=1369452#post1369452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stunts don't restore motes.<br /> Use Extras health levels on all NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thirded in both cases. As an option, you might want to implement a flat 5m regeneration per turn (as in 3e) to avoid mote depletion becoming the endgame of combat. Ignore Overdrive pools, or allow Overdrive requirements to become a splat-specific type of stunt instead, to reward interesting or risky combat tactics.<br /> <br /> That more than makes up for stunts not giving any points back, and frees stunts up for heroics and measured risk-taking rather than something you absolutely have to do to stay alive.<br /> <br /> One common houserule I see is to give every character (Essence) levels of Ox-Body Technique or its alternatives. It avoids TPKs and makes perfects less necessary. It means players are less worried about making their characters completely invulnerable too. The downside is that it may prolong combat. <br /> <br /> An alternative would be to rule that a PC cannot accidentally die and allow them to lose a dot in an Attribute instead (usually Physical, but potentially also Appearance, Wits, Perception, etc), as a sort of Crippling Injury, whenever they would ordinarily be killed.<br /> <br /> Finally, you could probably simplify combat by letting a PC attack which rolls 10 successes (I've not tested this yet; it might need to be slightly lower) always succeed, regardless of DV, perhaps with reduced damage as a trade-off (e.g., reduce damage by the difference between 10 and the actual DV). That potentially avoids NPCs with huge DVs withstanding multiple rounds of combat without a scratch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T16:32:33-08:00","id":1369922,"title":"","content":"Wow. There are a lot of great ideas here.<br /> <br /> Thank you, guys. This is really good stuff<br /> <br /> One quick Q:<br /> <br /> I was thinking to not roll Raw Damage Dice from successful attacks, but to just half the dice &amp; consider them Auto Successes to get rid of another roll.<br /> <br /> Does that sound logical?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T01:22:15-08:00","id":1369997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369318-best-ways-to-streamline-2nd-edition-combat-2-0-or-2-5?p=1369922#post1369922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. There are a lot of great ideas here.<br /> <br /> Thank you, guys. This is really good stuff<br /> <br /> One quick Q:<br /> <br /> I was thinking to not roll Raw Damage Dice from successful attacks, but to just half the dice &amp; consider them Auto Successes to get rid of another roll.<br /> <br /> Does that sound logical?</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC (I may be mixing up terminology), you don't roll the raw damage. You subtract the full soak first and then only roll whatever's left (net damage). Or at least, that's how we interpreted 2.5e damage.<br /> <br /> So:<br /> <br /> I roll 12 successes against my opponent's DV of 8. That means I get 4 threshold successes to carry over to damage. I'm using something big and deadly with 11 damage and my Strength is 3, so that's 11+3+4=18 raw damage.<br /> <br /> However, my opponent is a tough SOB, so his soak is 12. I subtract 12 from 18=6 net damage. I roll the 6 dice and get 2, 7, 8, 6, 3, 9 = 3 health levels (lethal in this case, because I used an edged weapon).<br /> <br /> That gets applied straight to the character's health track as X X X. Job done.<br /> <br /> You certainly could just halve net damage at the end, but you'll lose some unpredictability. That may not be the end of the world.<br /> <br /> In the example above, I might have only rolled one success or I might have rolled six. If I rolled zero, my weapon probably has a minimum damage (damage ping) of at least 1.<br /> <br /> If you only halve the damage, combat is more predictable, which is generally good. However, PCs may struggle to cause lethal blows to greater NPCs, too, which may or may not be a problem, depending on who they go up against. <br /> <br /> Another option is to roll PC damage but just average NPC damage? Or only roll damage where it's dramatically appropriate (e.g., in a typical 'Boss Fight' scenario where every health level inflicted counts).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 02-24-2020, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T02:47:03-08:00","id":1370280,"title":"","content":"I believe you are correct &amp; I was wrong. It is Net Damage, not Raw.<br /> <br /> I'm currently considering not bothering with Knock-back unless a Player wishes to utilize it.<br /> <br /> Would combat would suffer for that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T04:11:34-08:00","id":1370299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369318-best-ways-to-streamline-2nd-edition-combat-2-0-or-2-5?p=1370280#post1370280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe you are correct &amp; I was wrong. It is Net Damage, not Raw.<br /> <br /> I'm currently considering not bothering with Knock-back unless a Player wishes to utilize it.<br /> <br /> Would combat would suffer for that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah knock-back isn't essential.<br /> <br /> There's a rule for minions or objects for not rolling damage: you could use those.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T10:43:01-08:00","id":1370399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369318-best-ways-to-streamline-2nd-edition-combat-2-0-or-2-5?p=1370299#post1370299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah knock-back isn't essential.<br /> <br /> There's a rule for minions or objects for not rolling damage: you could use those.</div> </div> </div> </div>We mostly ignore it too. If a PC has a Charm that uses it, we'll use it on an NPC. Otherwise, it never comes up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T10:44:45-08:00","id":1370400,"title":"","content":"Oh, and 2.5e doesn't let most armour stack. That really speeds up the buying of goodies. People aren't juggling loads of items and trinkets to maximise their bonuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}